{ Your London set-up is complete. Against his quiet b6, you would simply castle. He can also prepare the e pawn push with a rook move or a queen move. }
8... Re8 { His rook comes to e8, right behind the pawn he wants to push to e5. If it gets there, your wall starts to shake. [%csl Re8] } 9. Ne5 { Right: your knight takes e5 first, so his pawn can never go there. [%csl Ge5] } (9. O-O { Castling first lets him play e5 at once. } 9... e5 10. dxe5 Nxe5 11. Bxe5 Bxe5 12. Nxe5 Rxe5 { Level: he got his e5 push in, the pieces came off, and his game is free. [%csl Re5] }) (9. Be5 { The bishop takes the square instead, and he can swap it off whenever he likes. } 9... b6 10. O-O { Level: your bishop on e5 is fine, but it is not planted there for good. [%csl Be5] }) (9. Qc2 { The queen comes out, but e5 is still free for him. } 9... e5 10. dxe5 Nxe5 { About level: his e5 push arrived, and his pieces are active. [%csl Re5] }) 9... Qc7 { His queen lines up behind his bishop on d6, both aiming at your knight. Had he taken on e5, your d pawn would take back and kick his knight. [%cal Rc7e5] } 10. f4 { The f pawn props your knight up: it now stands on e5 guarded by two pawns, and his e5 push is gone for good. [%cal Gf4e5,Gd4e5] } (10. Nxc6 { Just as good: trade knights and put your bishop on e5. } 10... Qxc6 11. Be5 { Slightly better for you: the bishop took the e5 square instead of the knight. [%csl Ge5] }) (10. Ndf3 { Also good: your other knight backs up e5. } 10... Bd7 11. O-O { About level: the knight holds on e5, but your f pawn would have propped it up more firmly. [%csl Ge5] }) (10. Nef3 { Stepping back gives him the e5 square after all. } 10... Bxg3 11. hxg3 e5 { Slightly better for him: his e5 push arrived, and your knight wasted two moves. [%csl Re5] }) (10. Bb5 { The pin is playable, but he swaps off your knight. } 10... Bd7 11. Nxd7 Nxd7 { Level: the knight on e5 is gone, and e5 is free for him again. [%csl Re5] }) (10. O-O { Castling ignores the pressure on e5. } 10... Nxe5 11. dxe5 Bxe5 { A pawn down: the knights came off, and his bishop picked up your pawn on e5. [%csl Re5] }) 1-0


